<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
==Description==
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
The '''Clone''' tool creates a linked copy of a selected object which will follow any future edits to the original object (except placement). For example, one use case is when you want to do [[PartDesign_Boolean|PartDesign Boolean]] on an object created in another workbench. Most types of objects are accepted, as long as they are solids. If you need to clone multiple objects (i.e., bodies) or a [[Std_Part|Part Container]], you may use [[Draft_Clone|Draft Workbench's clone]]. One caveat is that the Part Design Workbench's clone sets the current placement of the clone as zero (both Cartesian translation and spatial orientations). While the Draft's workbenches clone calculates and sets the numerical values of the current placement and orientation of the cloned objects with respect to the cloned object container.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
The '''Clone''' tool can clone specific features of a [[PartDesign_Body|PartDesign Body]] or base objects for those features (e.g. sketches). The cloned object will be created hierarchically inside a separate Body.
</div>

[[File:clone.png|400px]]
<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{Caption|Clone of the pin while being translated in 3D space as an independent object}}
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
==Usage==
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
# In the Tree View, select the object to be cloned.
# There are several ways to invoke the tool:
#* Press the {{Button|[[File:PartDesign_Clone.svg|16px]] [[PartDesign_Clone|Clone]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Part Design → [[Image:PartDesign_Clone.svg|16px]] Clone}} option from the menu.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
==Properties==
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* {{PropertyData|Base Feature}}: sets the original object the clone is based on. To replace, press the {{Button|…}} button to get a list of available objects. Changing this property now correctly preserves the clone's display and computed placement instead of showing incorrect geometry. Positioning the source object at a specific location before cloning can be used to control the shape's placement relative to the Clone's origin. {{Version|26.3}}
* {{PropertyData|Placement}}: defines the orientation and position of the Clone in the 3D space. See [[Placement|Placement]].
* {{PropertyData|Label}}: label given to the Clone object. Change to suit your needs.
</div>


